From 5d2421fea28916f5fe6dd4bf12c20e7ba9d18178 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.net>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:46:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] bcm2835-hdmiaudiod: the vc5 HDMI ports of the BCM2711 (Pi 4,
 Pi 400)

The same audio path at other offsets: per-port MAI registers in the shared
HD block, the core at 0x7ef00700 (HDMI0) or 0x7ef05700 (HDMI1), packet RAM
in its own block, 4-bit channel map, gen-5 MAI thresholds, DREQ 10 for
HDMI0. The sample clock comes from the fixed 108 MHz audio clock, the pixel
clock from the port PHY PLL. The driver takes the port the firmware sends
video on, and leaves a port alone whose DVP reset is held or whose clock
is stopped. QEMU raspi4b aborts reads of the DVP block, so a child
process (--probe-dvp) reads it first. It powers up the PHY random
generator, as Linux does.

Address translation goes through /soc ranges and dma-ranges with their
real cell counts (one address cell below /soc, two above on the BCM2711).

Refs redox-rpi/redox-rpi#543.
