 //! into HDMI audio packets.
 //!
+//! The BCM2711 (Pi 4, Pi 400) has the same audio path in its two "vc5" HDMI
+//! ports, at other offsets (`Regs`): a shared HD block (bus 0x7ef20000) with
+//! one MAI FIFO per port, the core of each port, and a separate packet RAM
+//! block. Its audio clock is a fixed 108 MHz, and the pixel clock comes from
+//! the port's PHY PLL (`pixel_from_vc5_phy`), as Linux `vc4_hdmi_regs.h`
+//! (`vc5_hdmi_hdmi0_fields`, `vc5_hdmi_hdmi1_fields`) and `vc4_hdmi_phy.c`
+//! have them.
+//!
